#include <stddef.h>

void untransform(uint8_t *buf, size_t len, const uint8_t *table) {
    if (len == 0) return;

    for (size_t i = 0; i < len; i++) {
        uint8_t val = buf[i];
        uint8_t key = table[i & 7];

        // Reverse the rotation: ROL 3 -> ROR 3
        val = (val >> 3) | (val << 5);

        // Reverse the XOR
        val ^= key;

        buf[i] = val;
    }
}
```

**Key Insight:** Since XOR is its own inverse ($a \oplus k \oplus k = a$) and rotation is also its own inverse when applied in the opposite direction (or the complementary direction modulo 8), applying the exact same logic but with **ROR 3** instead of **ROL 3** will restore the original data.

